# Route the @astro-mine scope to GitHub Packages, where this workspace's packages publish during
# private incubation. Today every @astro-mine dependency here is `workspace:*` and resolves locally,
# so a clean install — including CI's — needs no credential at all (CX-LOCAL). This mapping is what
# makes the *published* packages installable by a consumer, and it is safe to commit.
#
# Auth is supplied at the *user* level, never here — pnpm deliberately ignores an `_authToken` in a
# committed project .npmrc, because a swapped registry line could otherwise leak a secret to an
# attacker-controlled registry. Provide it via:
#   pnpm config set "//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken" "$(gh auth token)"   # locally, once (read:packages)
# In CI, actions/setup-node (registry-url + scope) writes a trusted user-level npmrc from NODE_AUTH_TOKEN.
@astro-mine:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
